{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WM4ovDfiXyGfgeFXLVzZzZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — distill_sparse_swiglu\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 2026 cycle)\n5\t- Deadline: 2026-05-25 (ARR submission)\n6\t- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims\n9\t\n10\t1. **KL distillation discovers fundamentally different (and superior) neuron importance patterns that magnitude-based oracles miss**: The C1 causal ablation (D059) proves that KL's advantage comes **entirely** from target quality (which neurons to keep), with gradient coupling contributing ≈0 across **both PPL and all downstream tasks**. **Controlled eval (TEAL 50% uniform, matched protocol)**: BCE+KL-targets PPL = **11.9638**, KL predictor PPL = **11.9638** (exact match). **Downstream confirmation (full-spectrum)**: All 4 downstream tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K) also match within <1pp delta, confirming gradient coupling = 0 across PPL + reasoning + knowledge + math dimensions. Standard BCE (magnitude masks) PPL ≈ 22.51. Target quality alone accounts for KL's full advantage. *Additional evidence from training eval (Gumbel hard mask)*: BCE+KL-targets PPL 9.29 @60.9% ≈ KL 9.21 @60.6%, consistent with controlled eval. The 53% mask divergence between KL-derived and magnitude-based masks is the core empirical finding: KL discovers a qualitatively different neuron importance landscape. **Implication**: The gradient coupling analysis (§3.6) provides mathematical intuition for *why* KL can discover better targets (coupled gradients explore joint neuron interaction patterns), but the causal driver is the resulting mask quality, not the gradient pathway per se. This shifts the contribution from \"engineering a better loss\" to \"discovering that output-distribution distillation reveals hidden neuron importance structure.\" **Supporting evidence**: (a) Iso-compute ablation: BCE with 2.71× more FLOPs still PPL=27.97 vs KL=12.00, confirming the gap is structural; (b) BCE at recommended 30% operating point (D062): forced TEAL top-k PPL=11.24 vs KL=8.82, Δ=2.42 — BCE 30% is nearly as bad as KL 50% (11.80), meaning BCE's inferior masks waste ~20pp of sparsity budget; (c) BCE Lagrangian failure at 30%: BCE loss scale (~0.6) vs KL (~0.0001) causes same Lagrangian to fail; (d) No compensation needed: KL eliminates 67.2M compensation parameters (~256MB). **Anticipated attack**: \"Two-stage training (KL→oracle→BCE) avoids needing KL predictor at inference?\" Defense: KL predictor is contextual (per-input adaptive); oracle masks are fixed. Deployment requires per-input sparsity adaptation. **Remaining caveat**: Single seed (s42); C1 s123 in progress for statistical robustness. (Headline claim, resolves persistent R3-R8 confound)\n11\t\n12\t2. **SPON's static correction is orthogonal to KL and too weak to complement it**: Logit-space decomposition (plan_005) shows SPON's bias correction is near-orthogonal to KL's mask effect (cos_sim=0.196, per-layer ≤0) with only 15.8% relative magnitude. Cross-layer interaction is non-trivial (30.6%) but PPL recovery remains modest (7.3%, 0.23 PPL). Rather than KL \"subsuming\" SPON, the two target different error components—but SPON's component is too small to provide meaningful complementary benefit. Strengthens Claim 1: static correction is not just redundant but irrelevant to the dominant error mode that KL addresses. (Evidence: plan_005_subsumption_s42, spon_2048_s42, D009, D010)\n13\t\n14\t3. **Sparsity regime determines whether allocation or capacity is the bottleneck (phase transition finding)**: Empirical discovery from D030 uniform allocation experiments reveals a qualitative phase transition, not the originally predicted quadratic scaling. At ≤30% sparsity, global top-k causes high seed-to-seed variance in downstream metrics due to per-layer allocation imbalance (uniform allocation stabilizes MMLU: σ drops from 9.5pp to 1.3pp across 3 seeds, mean 40.7% vs TEAL's 38.6%). At ≥50%, model capacity itself is insufficient — no allocation strategy can recover (uniform MMLU=27.8%≈random). The transition reveals three distinct regimes with non-monotonic allocation preference: (1) **Budget-surplus regime (≤30%)**: uniform allocation reduces seed-to-seed instability by 7.5× (σ: 1.3pp vs 9.5pp across 3 seeds), stabilizing downstream performance (3-seed mean MMLU: 40.7±1.3pp uniform vs 35.7±9.5pp global); (2) **Budget-constrained regime (~40%)**: learned allocation outperforms blind uniformity — MMLU 38.1% (global) vs 30.7% (uniform), +7.4pp — the predictor's learned priorities become valuable when budget is tight; (3) **Capacity-cliff regime (≥50%)**: allocation irrelevant, both collapse to ~28% ≈ random. Recommended operating point (8B-validated): 30% sparsity with uniform allocation. At 30%, KL uniform dominates on the efficiency-quality Pareto frontier: PPL 8.82 vs TEAL 10.97 (−19.6%), with comparable-to-better downstream (MMLU +2.0pp, WG +2.5pp; ARC-c −1.5pp, GSM8K −0.5pp within noise). The advantage is primarily in PPL and knowledge-intensive tasks, not uniform across all benchmarks. **14B scale-dependent caveat (D054)**: At Qwen-2.5-14B 50% sparsity, uniform allocation does NOT fix KL's MMLU gap (64.49% uniform vs 63.72% global, only +0.77pp; TEAL global=71.83%). The 8B allocation-dependent pattern does not generalize to 14B. This is a valuable negative finding revealing loss × allocation × scale three-way interaction. 14B claim scope: KL PPL advantage preserved (7.62 vs 8.73 TEAL), but downstream MMLU gap persists regardless of allocation. The non-monotonic allocation preference (uniform@30% → global@40% → irrelevant@50%) provides mechanistic insight: at generous budgets, ensuring no layer is starved matters most; at tight budgets, the predictor's learned cross-layer priorities add value; at catastrophic budgets, capacity itself is the binding constraint. The failure mode changes qualitatively: allocation-fixable (≤30%) vs capacity-limited (≥50%). PPL non-monotonicity (40%=8.36 < 30%=8.82) while downstream is strictly monotonic further supports \"PPL is a poor proxy for downstream quality\" narrative. **6-point PPL regime curve (D063)**: 30%=8.82, 35%=9.31, 40%=10.12, 45%=10.80, 50%=11.80 (TEAL global). Smooth monotonic increase from 30-50%, providing dense sampling for regime boundary identification. 25% eval pending. This yields a practical deployment guideline and a mechanistic understanding of when/why sparse inference degrades. (Evidence: d030_kl30_uniform, d030_kl50_uniform, d030_kl40_uniform, bench_teal30, bench_teal50, bench_kl30_global, bench_kl50_global, lm_eval downstream series)\n15\t\n16\t## Story Spine\n17\t\n18\t- **Problem**: SwiGLU activation sparsity enables 40-60% neuron pruning at inference, but training-free heuristics (WINA/TEAL) leave a 6+ point quality gap, while learned BCE predictors require auxiliary compensation networks adding ~256MB overhead (FastForward).\n19\t\n20\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: (a) Training-free (WINA, TEAL, R-Sparse): no training cost, but quality gap too large for deployment. (b) Static learned (SPON): zero-overhead bias correction via KL distillation, but input-independent — cannot adapt to per-input neuron importance. (c) Contextual learned (FastForward): BCE predictor + compensation MLP, near-dense quality but inference overhead from compensation network. Gap: no prior work trains the contextual predictor itself with KL, and no work quantifies how much static correction remains useful once a coupled-loss contextual predictor is in place.\n21\t\n22\t- **Our framing / headline question**: \"What does KL distillation actually learn for SwiGLU sparsity prediction, and why do its masks differ fundamentally from magnitude-based oracles?\" The theoretical grounding (§3.6, suggestive): BCE gradient dL_BCE/ds_j depends only on neuron j (factorized), while KL gradient dL_KL/ds_j couples all active neurons through d_logits/dh * dh/dm. This provides intuition for how KL *can* discover joint interaction patterns. The C1 causal ablation (§4.4) then empirically confirms: the masks KL discovers, not the gradient pathway itself, are what matter.\n23\t\n24\t- **Headline result template**: \"KL-trained sparsity predictors discover neuron importance patterns that diverge 53% from magnitude-based masks. A causal ablation confirms that these mask patterns, not gradient coupling, drive KL's quality advantage: BCE trained on KL-derived masks matches KL performance exactly across PPL (11.96 = 11.96) and all downstream tasks (delta <1pp on ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K). This finding eliminates the need for 67.2M compensation parameters and reveals three sparsity operating regimes (now with 6 data points) with qualitatively different allocation requirements.\"\n25\t\n26\t## Two-Dimensional Taxonomy (Conceptual Contribution)\n27\t\n28\t|                          | Decomposed (BCE) | Intermediate (MSE) | Coupled (KL) |\n29\t|--------------------------|:-----------------:|:-------------------:|:-------------:|\n30\t| Static                   | —                 | —                   | SPON          |\n31\t| Per-layer                | —                 | ShadowLLM           | —             |\n32\t| Per-token contextual     | FastForward       | —                   | **Ours**      |\n33\t\n34\tPositions prior work and ours on two axes: correction granularity (static -> per-token) x training signal coupling (decomposed/BCE -> coupled/KL). Highlights the empty cell we fill.\n35\t\n36\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n37\t\n38\t1. **\"Incremental / no new algorithm\"**: **Substantially mitigated by C1 finding**. The 53% mask divergence and causal ablation are genuine empirical discoveries, not engineering contributions. No prior work has shown that KL-derived masks encode fundamentally different neuron importance from magnitude-based approaches. The paper now contributes a finding (mask pattern discovery) rather than just a method (combining known techniques). Additional support: formal decomposition framework, quantitative s^2 prediction, three-regime analysis.\n39\t\n40\t2. **\"KL wins only because more compute\"**: **Fully addressed** by iso-compute ablation (eval_bce_v3_s42): BCE with 2.71× more FLOPs → TEAL PPL=27.97 vs KL=12.00 (2.33× gap). BCE loss saturates, confirming structural mismatch not compute deficit.\n41\t\n42\t3. **\"Gumbel-sigmoid relaxation, not KL, explains gains\"**: Addressed by STE baseline (plan_002) isolating loss function contribution.\n43\t\n44\t4. **\"Single model / limited generalization\"**: Addressed by Mistral-7B-v0.3 (plan_009, GQA + sliding window) and Qwen-2.5-14B cross-scale validation (D048/D054). **14B mixed result**: KL PPL advantage preserved (7.62 vs TEAL 8.73, 1.47× dense ratio identical to 8B), but KL MMLU=63.72% (global) / 64.49% (uniform) significantly trails TEAL 71.83% (global). Uniform allocation does not fix this gap (D054). PPL-downstream disconnect at 14B scale is an honest limitation, not hidden. Framing: KL's coupled gradient captures output-distribution fidelity (PPL) across scales, but 14B knowledge-intensive tasks (MMLU) show scale-dependent sensitivity that warrants further investigation.\n45\t\n46\t5. **\"Effect size may not hold on downstream tasks\"**: Core defense: PPL + 4 discriminative tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K) under unified few-shot protocol across all conditions. LongBench (P1, if GPU budget allows) strengthens long-context coverage. MT-Bench deferred unless time permits — requires external LLM API for judging.\n47\t\n48\t6. **\"Unfair comparison: BCE+comp close to KL but at higher inference cost\"**: All result tables and figures must co-report quality AND inference cost (compensation params, per-token FLOPs, end-to-end latency). Efficiency-accuracy Pareto frontier (plan_007) is the definitive visualization. Even if BCE+comp matches KL on PPL, KL wins on the Pareto frontier — that IS the claim.\n49\t\n50\t## Venue Fit\n51\t- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: strong fit for activation sparsity + distillation\n52\t- NLP-specific evaluation (LongBench long-context, MT-Bench multi-turn) strengthens EMNLP fit vs pure systems venue\n53\t- **Novelty upgraded from R8**: C1 causal ablation + 53% mask divergence finding elevates paper from \"systematic composition\" to \"empirical discovery about what KL learns for sparsity prediction.\" This addresses the persistent R3-R8 novelty concern and moves the paper toward Main Conference territory (target 4.0).\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a65ea5d-7d8b-45ad-b79b-73646d535216","uuid":"2b3244f3-d3c8-44a9-8f73-99d8a20c9ed9","timestamp":"2026-05-18T18:19:27.738Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T173518/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — distill_sparse_swiglu\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 2026 cycle)\n- Deadline: 2026-05-25 (ARR submission)\n- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n\n## Core Claims\n\n1. **KL distillation discovers fundamentally different (and superior) neuron importance patterns that magnitude-based oracles miss**: The C1 causal ablation (D059) proves that KL's advantage comes **entirely** from target quality (which neurons to keep), with gradient coupling contributing ≈0 across **both PPL and all downstream tasks**. **Controlled eval (TEAL 50% uniform, matched protocol)**: BCE+KL-targets PPL = **11.9638**, KL predictor PPL = **11.9638** (exact match). **Downstream confirmation (full-spectrum)**: All 4 downstream tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K) also match within <1pp delta, confirming gradient coupling = 0 across PPL + reasoning + knowledge + math dimensions. Standard BCE (magnitude masks) PPL ≈ 22.51. Target quality alone accounts for KL's full advantage. *Additional evidence from training eval (Gumbel hard mask)*: BCE+KL-targets PPL 9.29 @60.9% ≈ KL 9.21 @60.6%, consistent with controlled eval. The 53% mask divergence between KL-derived and magnitude-based masks is the core empirical finding: KL discovers a qualitatively different neuron importance landscape. **Implication**: The gradient coupling analysis (§3.6) provides mathematical intuition for *why* KL can discover better targets (coupled gradients explore joint neuron interaction patterns), but the causal driver is the resulting mask quality, not the gradient pathway per se. This shifts the contribution from \"engineering a better loss\" to \"discovering that output-distribution distillation reveals hidden neuron importance structure.\" **Supporting evidence**: (a) Iso-compute ablation: BCE with 2.71× more FLOPs still PPL=27.97 vs KL=12.00, confirming the gap is structural; (b) BCE at recommended 30% operating point (D062): forced TEAL top-k PPL=11.24 vs KL=8.82, Δ=2.42 — BCE 30% is nearly as bad as KL 50% (11.80), meaning BCE's inferior masks waste ~20pp of sparsity budget; (c) BCE Lagrangian failure at 30%: BCE loss scale (~0.6) vs KL (~0.0001) causes same Lagrangian to fail; (d) No compensation needed: KL eliminates 67.2M compensation parameters (~256MB). **Anticipated attack**: \"Two-stage training (KL→oracle→BCE) avoids needing KL predictor at inference?\" Defense: KL predictor is contextual (per-input adaptive); oracle masks are fixed. Deployment requires per-input sparsity adaptation. **Remaining caveat**: Single seed (s42); C1 s123 in progress for statistical robustness. (Headline claim, resolves persistent R3-R8 confound)\n\n2. **SPON's static correction is orthogonal to KL and too weak to complement it**: Logit-space decomposition (plan_005) shows SPON's bias correction is near-orthogonal to KL's mask effect (cos_sim=0.196, per-layer ≤0) with only 15.8% relative magnitude. Cross-layer interaction is non-trivial (30.6%) but PPL recovery remains modest (7.3%, 0.23 PPL). Rather than KL \"subsuming\" SPON, the two target different error components—but SPON's component is too small to provide meaningful complementary benefit. Strengthens Claim 1: static correction is not just redundant but irrelevant to the dominant error mode that KL addresses. (Evidence: plan_005_subsumption_s42, spon_2048_s42, D009, D010)\n\n3. **Sparsity regime determines whether allocation or capacity is the bottleneck (phase transition finding)**: Empirical discovery from D030 uniform allocation experiments reveals a qualitative phase transition, not the originally predicted quadratic scaling. At ≤30% sparsity, global top-k causes high seed-to-seed variance in downstream metrics due to per-layer allocation imbalance (uniform allocation stabilizes MMLU: σ drops from 9.5pp to 1.3pp across 3 seeds, mean 40.7% vs TEAL's 38.6%). At ≥50%, model capacity itself is insufficient — no allocation strategy can recover (uniform MMLU=27.8%≈random). The transition reveals three distinct regimes with non-monotonic allocation preference: (1) **Budget-surplus regime (≤30%)**: uniform allocation reduces seed-to-seed instability by 7.5× (σ: 1.3pp vs 9.5pp across 3 seeds), stabilizing downstream performance (3-seed mean MMLU: 40.7±1.3pp uniform vs 35.7±9.5pp global); (2) **Budget-constrained regime (~40%)**: learned allocation outperforms blind uniformity — MMLU 38.1% (global) vs 30.7% (uniform), +7.4pp — the predictor's learned priorities become valuable when budget is tight; (3) **Capacity-cliff regime (≥50%)**: allocation irrelevant, both collapse to ~28% ≈ random. Recommended operating point (8B-validated): 30% sparsity with uniform allocation. At 30%, KL uniform dominates on the efficiency-quality Pareto frontier: PPL 8.82 vs TEAL 10.97 (−19.6%), with comparable-to-better downstream (MMLU +2.0pp, WG +2.5pp; ARC-c −1.5pp, GSM8K −0.5pp within noise). The advantage is primarily in PPL and knowledge-intensive tasks, not uniform across all benchmarks. **14B scale-dependent caveat (D054)**: At Qwen-2.5-14B 50% sparsity, uniform allocation does NOT fix KL's MMLU gap (64.49% uniform vs 63.72% global, only +0.77pp; TEAL global=71.83%). The 8B allocation-dependent pattern does not generalize to 14B. This is a valuable negative finding revealing loss × allocation × scale three-way interaction. 14B claim scope: KL PPL advantage preserved (7.62 vs 8.73 TEAL), but downstream MMLU gap persists regardless of allocation. The non-monotonic allocation preference (uniform@30% → global@40% → irrelevant@50%) provides mechanistic insight: at generous budgets, ensuring no layer is starved matters most; at tight budgets, the predictor's learned cross-layer priorities add value; at catastrophic budgets, capacity itself is the binding constraint. The failure mode changes qualitatively: allocation-fixable (≤30%) vs capacity-limited (≥50%). PPL non-monotonicity (40%=8.36 < 30%=8.82) while downstream is strictly monotonic further supports \"PPL is a poor proxy for downstream quality\" narrative. **6-point PPL regime curve (D063)**: 30%=8.82, 35%=9.31, 40%=10.12, 45%=10.80, 50%=11.80 (TEAL global). Smooth monotonic increase from 30-50%, providing dense sampling for regime boundary identification. 25% eval pending. This yields a practical deployment guideline and a mechanistic understanding of when/why sparse inference degrades. (Evidence: d030_kl30_uniform, d030_kl50_uniform, d030_kl40_uniform, bench_teal30, bench_teal50, bench_kl30_global, bench_kl50_global, lm_eval downstream series)\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: SwiGLU activation sparsity enables 40-60% neuron pruning at inference, but training-free heuristics (WINA/TEAL) leave a 6+ point quality gap, while learned BCE predictors require auxiliary compensation networks adding ~256MB overhead (FastForward).\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: (a) Training-free (WINA, TEAL, R-Sparse): no training cost, but quality gap too large for deployment. (b) Static learned (SPON): zero-overhead bias correction via KL distillation, but input-independent — cannot adapt to per-input neuron importance. (c) Contextual learned (FastForward): BCE predictor + compensation MLP, near-dense quality but inference overhead from compensation network. Gap: no prior work trains the contextual predictor itself with KL, and no work quantifies how much static correction remains useful once a coupled-loss contextual predictor is in place.\n\n- **Our framing / headline question**: \"What does KL distillation actually learn for SwiGLU sparsity prediction, and why do its masks differ fundamentally from magnitude-based oracles?\" The theoretical grounding (§3.6, suggestive): BCE gradient dL_BCE/ds_j depends only on neuron j (factorized), while KL gradient dL_KL/ds_j couples all active neurons through d_logits/dh * dh/dm. This provides intuition for how KL *can* discover joint interaction patterns. The C1 causal ablation (§4.4) then empirically confirms: the masks KL discovers, not the gradient pathway itself, are what matter.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"KL-trained sparsity predictors discover neuron importance patterns that diverge 53% from magnitude-based masks. A causal ablation confirms that these mask patterns, not gradient coupling, drive KL's quality advantage: BCE trained on KL-derived masks matches KL performance exactly across PPL (11.96 = 11.96) and all downstream tasks (delta <1pp on ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K). This finding eliminates the need for 67.2M compensation parameters and reveals three sparsity operating regimes (now with 6 data points) with qualitatively different allocation requirements.\"\n\n## Two-Dimensional Taxonomy (Conceptual Contribution)\n\n|                          | Decomposed (BCE) | Intermediate (MSE) | Coupled (KL) |\n|--------------------------|:-----------------:|:-------------------:|:-------------:|\n| Static                   | —                 | —                   | SPON          |\n| Per-layer                | —                 | ShadowLLM           | —             |\n| Per-token contextual     | FastForward       | —                   | **Ours**      |\n\nPositions prior work and ours on two axes: correction granularity (static -> per-token) x training signal coupling (decomposed/BCE -> coupled/KL). Highlights the empty cell we fill.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"Incremental / no new algorithm\"**: **Substantially mitigated by C1 finding**. The 53% mask divergence and causal ablation are genuine empirical discoveries, not engineering contributions. No prior work has shown that KL-derived masks encode fundamentally different neuron importance from magnitude-based approaches. The paper now contributes a finding (mask pattern discovery) rather than just a method (combining known techniques). Additional support: formal decomposition framework, quantitative s^2 prediction, three-regime analysis.\n\n2. **\"KL wins only because more compute\"**: **Fully addressed** by iso-compute ablation (eval_bce_v3_s42): BCE with 2.71× more FLOPs → TEAL PPL=27.97 vs KL=12.00 (2.33× gap). BCE loss saturates, confirming structural mismatch not compute deficit.\n\n3. **\"Gumbel-sigmoid relaxation, not KL, explains gains\"**: Addressed by STE baseline (plan_002) isolating loss function contribution.\n\n4. **\"Single model / limited generalization\"**: Addressed by Mistral-7B-v0.3 (plan_009, GQA + sliding window) and Qwen-2.5-14B cross-scale validation (D048/D054). **14B mixed result**: KL PPL advantage preserved (7.62 vs TEAL 8.73, 1.47× dense ratio identical to 8B), but KL MMLU=63.72% (global) / 64.49% (uniform) significantly trails TEAL 71.83% (global). Uniform allocation does not fix this gap (D054). PPL-downstream disconnect at 14B scale is an honest limitation, not hidden. Framing: KL's coupled gradient captures output-distribution fidelity (PPL) across scales, but 14B knowledge-intensive tasks (MMLU) show scale-dependent sensitivity that warrants further investigation.\n\n5. **\"Effect size may not hold on downstream tasks\"**: Core defense: PPL + 4 discriminative tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K) under unified few-shot protocol across all conditions. LongBench (P1, if GPU budget allows) strengthens long-context coverage. MT-Bench deferred unless time permits — requires external LLM API for judging.\n\n6. **\"Unfair comparison: BCE+comp close to KL but at higher inference cost\"**: All result tables and figures must co-report quality AND inference cost (compensation params, per-token FLOPs, end-to-end latency). Efficiency-accuracy Pareto frontier (plan_007) is the definitive visualization. Even if BCE+comp matches KL on PPL, KL wins on the Pareto frontier — that IS the claim.\n\n## Venue Fit\n- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: strong fit for activation sparsity + distillation\n- NLP-specific evaluation (LongBench long-context, MT-Bench multi-turn) strengthens EMNLP fit vs pure systems venue\n- **Novelty upgraded from R8**: C1 causal ablation + 53% mask divergence finding elevates paper from \"systematic composition\" to \"empirical discovery about what KL learns for sparsity prediction.\" This addresses the persistent R3-R8 novelty concern and moves the paper toward Main Conference territory (target 4.0).\n","numLines":54,"startLine":1,"totalLines":54}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RBFvorBCpJ9kZWz5nYYT88","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"c1_ablation_replication_3seed\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"C1 causal ablation 的 s123 retry 和 s456 新实验。训练 BCE predictor 使用各 seed 的 KL-derived oracle mask 作为 target，\\n在 TEAL uniform 50% 协议下评估，与对应 seed 的 KL predictor 对比。验证 s42 exact match 是否跨 seed 复现。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"s123_bce_kl_targets_ppl_teal_uniform_50pct\": 12.71,\n7\t      \"s123_kl_reference_ppl_teal_uniform_50pct\": 11.86,\n8\t      \"s123_ppl_delta\": 0.85,\n9\t      \"s123_oracle_agreement\": 0.921,\n10\t      \"s123_train_bce_loss\": 0.072,\n11\t      \"s123_arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.345,\n12\t      \"s123_winogrande_acc\": 0.598,\n13\t      \"s123_mmlu_acc\": 0.253,\n14\t      \"s123_gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.015,\n15\t      \"s123_downstream_ref_arc_c\": 0.379,\n16\t      \"s123_downstream_ref_wg\": 0.622,\n17\t      \"s123_downstream_ref_mmlu\": 0.278,\n18\t      \"s123_downstream_ref_gsm8k\": 0.024,\n19\t      \"s123_max_downstream_delta_pp\": 3.4,\n20\t      \"s456_bce_kl_targets_ppl_teal_uniform_50pct\": 12.55,\n21\t      \"s456_kl_reference_ppl_teal_uniform_50pct\": 11.95,\n22\t      \"s456_ppl_delta\": 0.6,\n23\t      \"s456_oracle_agreement\": 0.943,\n24\t      \"s456_train_bce_loss\": 0.063,\n25\t      \"s456_arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.362,\n26\t      \"s456_winogrande_acc\": 0.612,\n27\t      \"s456_mmlu_acc\": 0.268,\n28\t      \"s456_gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.019,\n29\t      \"s456_max_downstream_delta_pp\": 2.1,\n30\t      \"three_seed_ppl_deltas\": [\n31\t        0.0,\n32\t        0.85,\n33\t        0.6\n34\t      ],\n35\t      \"three_seed_ppl_delta_mean\": 0.48,\n36\t      \"three_seed_ppl_delta_std\": 0.36,\n37\t      \"three_seed_oracle_agreement_mean\": 0.947,\n38\t      \"three_seed_oracle_agreement_std\": 0.024,\n39\t      \"three_seed_max_downstream_delta_pp\": 3.4,\n40\t      \"gradient_coupling_contribution_range_pct\": \"0–18%\"\n41\t    },\n42\t    \"tables\": [\n43\t      \"Table 3: C1 Causal Ablation（3 seeds，PPL + 4 downstream tasks，含 oracle agreement）\"\n44\t    ],\n45\t    \"figures\": [],\n46\t    \"analysis\": \"C1 从 \\\"clean decomposition proving gradient coupling = 0\\\" 降级为 \\\"target quality is dominant but gradient coupling\\ncontribution is seed-dependent (0–18%)\\\"。论文需要：(1) 诚实报告 3 seed 及 variance；(2) 放弃 \\\"sole driver\\\" 措辞，\\n改为 \\\"primary driver, explaining 82–100% of advantage\\\"；(3) 将 seed 依赖性本身作为 finding 讨论——mask landscape\\n的局部结构决定了 gradient coupling 的边际贡献。C1 仍有价值（first attempt at causal decomposition for sparsity\\npredictor training loss），但 novelty 从 \\\"empirical discovery\\\" 降为 \\\"informative ablation with nuanced outcome\\\"。\\n审稿人会说 \\\"interesting but not conclusive\\\"。\\n\\n\\ns42 的 exact match（Δ=0.00）是 seed-specific 的幸运结果：s42 的 KL predictor 收敛到的局部最优产生了\\n\\\"clean\\\" mask pattern——borderline zone（gate probability 0.4–0.6）的 neuron 比例低（~8%），使 BCE 的\\nfactorized loss 足以高精度复制。s123 的 KL predictor 收敛到了不同局部最优，borderline neuron 比例更高（~14%），\\n这些 neuron 的重要性依赖于与其他 neuron 的共激活模式（joint interaction），BCE 无法捕捉。oracle agreement\\n从 0.978 降至 0.921，6% 的 mask 分歧集中在 knowledge-critical 中间层（L12–L20），导致 ARC-c 推理任务\\n出现 3.4pp gap。s456 介于两者之间（agreement 0.943，Δ=0.60），表明 gradient coupling 贡献是 loss landscape\\n局部结构的函数。3-seed 平均 Δ=0.48 技术上 <0.5，但 s123 的 0.85 无法被 error bar 掩盖，审稿人会质疑\\n\\\"gradient coupling = 0\\\" 的普遍性声明。\\n\"\n47\t  },\n48\t  {\n49\t    \"name\": \"bce_30pct_forced_topk_eval\",\n50\t    \"description\": \"BCE predictor（trained at 30% target on Llama-3.1-8B）通过 forced TEAL top-k 在 30% uniform sparsity 下评估。\\n填充 Table 2 的 BCE 30% operating point 数据。对比 KL 30% uniform（PPL 8.82）和 TEAL 30%（PPL 10.97）。\\n\",\n51\t    \"results\": {\n52\t      \"wikitext2_ppl_teal_uniform_30pct\": 9.15,\n53\t      \"gap_vs_kl30_uniform\": 0.33,\n54\t      \"gap_vs_teal30\": -1.82,\n55\t      \"arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.401,\n56\t      \"winogrande_acc\": 0.668,\n57\t      \"mmlu_acc\": 0.378,\n58\t      \"gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.062,\n59\t      \"ref_kl30_uniform_ppl\": 8.82,\n60\t      \"ref_kl30_uniform_mmlu\": 0.385,\n61\t      \"ref_kl30_uniform_arc_c\": 0.443,\n62\t      \"ref_kl30_uniform_wg\": 0.692,\n63\t      \"mmlu_gap_vs_kl30_pp\": -0.7,\n64\t      \"arc_c_gap_vs_kl30_pp\": -4.2,\n65\t      \"wg_gap_vs_kl30_pp\": -2.4,\n66\t      \"predictor_native_sparsity\": 0.295,\n67\t      \"lagrangian_converged\": true\n68\t    },\n69\t    \"tables\": [\n70\t      \"Table 2: Recommended Operating Point Comparison（30% sparsity, all methods）\",\n71\t      \"Table 1: Main Results（增加 BCE 30% 行）\"\n72\t    ],\n73\t    \"figures\": [],\n74\t    \"analysis\": \"BCE 30% PPL 9.15 vs KL 8.82（Δ=0.33, 3.7%）在 recommended operating point 实质追平。这削弱了 \\\"KL discovers\\nfundamentally different masks\\\" 作为 practical advantage 的叙事——在用户最可能部署的 sparsity level 上，\\n简单的 BCE + magnitude oracle 就足够好。KL 的优势主要体现在 ≥40% 的高 sparsity 区间，而该区间的 downstream\\ncollapse（MMLU ~31%）使其本身缺乏部署价值。\\nReframe: KL 的价值不在于 \\\"better masks at all sparsity levels\\\"，而在于 (a) 自动发现 good mask（zero-shot,\\n无需预定义 oracle），(b) 在高 sparsity 区间提供 graceful degradation 而非 catastrophic collapse，\\n(c) 跨 sparsity level 的 single training recipe（一个 KL predictor 可在 30–50% 间灵活部署，而 BCE 需要\\nper-level oracle 设计）。\\n\\n\\n30% sparsity 下 magnitude-based mask 与 optimal mask 的重合度远高于 50%（Jaccard ~0.6 vs ~0.4），因为\\n需要剪除的 neuron 大多是 \\\"trivially unimportant\\\"（activation magnitude 极低 + gate probability 极低），\\nBCE 和 KL 在这些 easy case 上完全一致。KL 的 joint interaction 优势只在 borderline neurons 上体现，而\\n30% 时 borderline zone 极窄（仅需剪除最不重要的 30%，几乎没有 hard decision）。PPL gap 从 50% 时的\\n~14 PPL（22.51 vs 8.82, 对比 BCE 50% vs KL 30%）收缩到 30% 时的 0.33，确认 KL-BCE delta 随 sparsity\\n近似二次收缩。BCE Lagrangian 在 8B 30% target 下正常收敛（不像 Qwen-14B 的 collapse），因为 30%\\n目标松弛、loss landscape smooth。下游任务 gap 最大 4.2pp（ARC-c），在 3-seed KL variance 范围内。\\n审稿人会看到 Table 2 中 KL 和 BCE 在 recommended operating point 几乎没有差别，质疑 KL 的实际部署价值。\\n\"\n75\t  },\n76\t  {\n77\t    \"name\": \"dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\",\n78\t    \"description\": \"KL predictor 在 25%/30%/35%/40%/45%/50% 六个 sparsity level 的 TEAL uniform 评估。\\n使用各 level 的 dedicated predictor（25/35/45 为新训练，30/40/50 复用已有）。\\n生成 regime curve 并尝试识别 regime boundary。\\n\",\n79\t    \"results\": {\n80\t      \"ppl_25pct\": 8.9,\n81\t      \"ppl_30pct\": 8.82,\n82\t      \"ppl_35pct\": 8.55,\n83\t      \"ppl_40pct\": 8.36,\n84\t      \"ppl_45pct\": 10.25,\n85\t      \"ppl_50pct\": 11.96,\n86\t      \"monotonicity_violations_ppl\": 3,\n87\t      \"ppl_global_25pct\": 9.05,\n88\t      \"ppl_global_30pct\": 8.98,\n89\t      \"ppl_global_35pct\": 8.7,\n90\t      \"ppl_global_40pct\": 10.12,\n91\t      \"ppl_global_45pct\": 10.9,\n92\t      \"ppl_global_50pct\": 11.79,\n93\t      \"monotonicity_violations_ppl_global\": 2,\n94\t      \"mmlu_25pct\": 0.39,\n95\t      \"mmlu_30pct\": 0.406,\n96\t      \"mmlu_35pct\": 0.415,\n97\t      \"mmlu_40pct\": 0.307,\n98\t      \"mmlu_45pct\": 0.282,\n99\t      \"mmlu_50pct\": 0.278,\n100\t      \"mmlu_monotonicity_violations\": 2,\n101\t      \"arc_c_25pct\": 0.43,\n102\t      \"arc_c_30pct\": 0.408,\n103\t      \"arc_c_35pct\": 0.44,\n104\t      \"arc_c_40pct\": 0.418,\n105\t      \"arc_c_45pct\": 0.35,\n106\t      \"arc_c_50pct\": 0.328,\n107\t      \"arc_c_monotonicity_violations\": 3,\n108\t      \"winogrande_25pct\": 0.7,\n109\t      \"winogrande_30pct\": 0.686,\n110\t      \"winogrande_35pct\": 0.705,\n111\t      \"winogrande_40pct\": 0.672,\n112\t      \"winogrande_45pct\": 0.64,\n113\t      \"winogrande_50pct\": 0.629,\n114\t      \"winogrande_monotonicity_violations\": 2,\n115\t      \"gsm8k_25pct\": 0.082,\n116\t      \"gsm8k_30pct\": 0.074,\n117\t      \"gsm8k_35pct\": 0.065,\n118\t      \"gsm8k_40pct\": 0.039,\n119\t      \"gsm8k_45pct\": 0.022,\n120\t      \"gsm8k_50pct\": 0.021,\n121\t      \"ppl_cliff_location\": \"40–45%\",\n122\t      \"mmlu_cliff_location\": \"35–40%\",\n123\t      \"cliff_dissociation\": \"PPL 和 MMLU 的 cliff 位于不同 sparsity level，间隔约 5pp\"\n124\t    },\n125\t    \"tables\": [\n126\t      \"Table 5: 6-Point Sparsity Regime Analysis（PPL + 4 downstream, uniform + global allocation）\"\n127\t    ],\n128\t    \"figures\": [],\n129\t    \"analysis\": \"Regime analysis 从 Claim 3 的核心贡献降级为 supplementary empirical characterization。原始叙事\\n\\\"three discrete regimes (budget-surplus / budget-constrained / capacity-cliff) with non-monotonic allocation\\npreference\\\" 被替换为：(a) continuous degradation with a PPL sweet spot around 35–40%；(b) PPL-downstream\\ndissociation 作为 finding（PPL cliff at 40–45%, MMLU cliff at 35–40%）；(c) practical recommendation\\n不变（30% uniform），但理由从 \\\"optimal regime 1 operating point\\\" 改为 \\\"safety margin below cliff\\\"。\\nNon-monotonicity 可 spin 为 \\\"dedicated-predictor optimization effect\\\"（each sparsity level has its own\\ntraining sweet spot），但审稿人可能视为 experimental noise 或 Lagrangian artifact。\\n建议在论文中补充 3-seed bars at 30/50 以佐证 known points 的 stability，并坦承 single-seed sweep\\n限制了 statistical confidence。\\n\\n\\nPPL 非单调性（25→40% 持续下降）的机制：dedicated predictor 在中等 sparsity（35–40%）达到 loss-sparsity 的\\n最佳平衡——Lagrangian 约束满足良好（actual sparsity 接近 target），KL loss 有足够的 \\\"budget\\\" 学习 nuanced\\nmask pattern。25% 时 predictor undertrained（actual 23%, lambda 打满 5000 仍不够），mask 质量反而不如\\n30% 的 well-calibrated predictor。35% 时 predictor 在 sweet spot（actual 33.6%, loss 收敛良好），\\n产生了比 30% 更优的 neuron ranking。40% 沿用 50%-trained predictor at 40% uniform（d030 数据），\\n该 predictor 在 40% 时仍有余量因此 PPL 最低。\\n\\n45→50% 的急剧上升反映 capacity cliff——不是 allocation 问题（都用 uniform），而是 model 容量不足。\\n但 MMLU 的 cliff 出现在 35→40%（Δ=10.8pp），比 PPL cliff（40→45%）早一个档位。这反映 knowledge-intensive\\ntasks（MMLU）对 neuron 缺失的敏感度高于 perplexity——PPL 可以靠 redistributing probability mass 补偿，\\n但 factual recall 一旦关键 neuron 被剪就不可逆。\\n\\n3 处 PPL monotonicity violation 使 \\\"three discrete regimes with phase transitions\\\" 叙事不可持续：\\n没有从 regime 1 到 regime 2 的 clean boundary，整个 25–40% 区间是一个 non-monotonic plateau。\\n审稿人会质疑 \\\"regime\\\" 分类的 principled basis。\\n\"\n130\t  },\n131\t  {\n132\t    \"name\": \"longbench_full_evaluation\",\n133\t    \"description\": \"LongBench English subset（14 tasks, 4K–32K tokens）评估所有条件：KL 30% uniform, KL 50%,\\nBCE+comp 30%, TEAL 30%, TEAL 50%, Dense。测试 predictor 在超出训练序列长度（2048）时的泛化能力。\\n\",\n134\t    \"results\": {\n135\t      \"dense_single_doc_qa_avg\": 10.8,\n136\t      \"dense_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 18.5,\n137\t      \"dense_summarization_avg\": 18.2,\n138\t      \"dense_few_shot_avg\": 36.0,\n139\t      \"dense_code_avg\": 31.5,\n140\t      \"dense_overall_avg\": 23.0,\n141\t      \"kl30_single_doc_qa_avg\": 5.8,\n142\t      \"kl30_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 9.5,\n143\t      \"kl30_summarization_avg\": 14.5,\n144\t      \"kl30_few_shot_avg\": 21.0,\n145\t      \"kl30_code_avg\": 19.0,\n146\t      \"kl30_overall_avg\": 14.0,\n147\t      \"kl30_retention_vs_dense\": 0.61,\n148\t      \"kl50_single_doc_qa_avg\": 2.2,\n149\t      \"kl50_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 3.8,\n150\t      \"kl50_summarization_avg\": 8.5,\n151\t      \"kl50_few_shot_avg\": 8.5,\n152\t      \"kl50_code_avg\": 9.0,\n153\t      \"kl50_overall_avg\": 6.4,\n154\t      \"kl50_retention_vs_dense\": 0.28,\n155\t      \"bce_comp_30_single_doc_qa_avg\": 5.2,\n156\t      \"bce_comp_30_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 8.8,\n157\t      \"bce_comp_30_summarization_avg\": 13.5,\n158\t      \"bce_comp_30_few_shot_avg\": 19.5,\n159\t      \"bce_comp_30_code_avg\": 17.5,\n160\t      \"bce_comp_30_overall_avg\": 12.9,\n161\t      \"bce_comp_30_retention_vs_dense\": 0.56,\n162\t      \"teal30_single_doc_qa_avg\": 4.2,\n163\t      \"teal30_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 7.2,\n164\t      \"teal30_summarization_avg\": 11.5,\n165\t      \"teal30_few_shot_avg\": 16.0,\n166\t      \"teal30_code_avg\": 15.0,\n167\t      \"teal30_overall_avg\": 10.8,\n168\t      \"teal30_retention_vs_dense\": 0.47,\n169\t      \"teal50_overall_avg\": 3.8,\n170\t      \"teal50_retention_vs_dense\": 0.17,\n171\t      \"kl30_vs_bce_comp30_delta\": 1.1,\n172\t      \"kl30_vs_teal30_delta\": 3.2,\n173\t      \"worst_category_kl30\": \"single-doc QA (-46%)\",\n174\t      \"best_category_kl30\": \"summarization (-20%)\"\n175\t    },\n176\t    \"tables\": [\n177\t      \"Table 5: LongBench Results by Task Category（5 categories × 6 conditions, retention % vs dense）\"\n178\t    ],\n179\t    \"figures\": [],\n180\t    \"analysis\": \"LongBench 结果 mixed：KL > TEAL（training-free）confirmed，但 KL vs BCE+comp 差异在 long-context 上\\n被压缩到不显著水平。Dense baseline 偏低限制了评估的 discriminative power。\\n对论文的影响：(1) 不宜作为 main contribution，降为 appendix 或简要提及；(2) 如果 reviewer 要求\\nlong-context evaluation，可呈现但需坦承 base model limitation 和 predictor generalization gap；\\n(3) 建议补充 \\\"predictor seq-len generalization\\\" 分析（对比 2048 vs 4096 训练长度的 predictor 在\\nLongBench 上的差异），但 GPU budget 可能不允许。\\n实际影响：plan_010 的 P1 优先级在 worst case 下应降为 P2，将 GPU hours 重新分配给更能 strengthen\\nnarrative 的实验（如 BCE 30% 的多 seed 验证）。\\n\\n\\nPredictor 在 2048 tokens 上训练，LongBench 任务平均 8K–16K tokens。超出训练长度后 predictor 的\\nneuron importance judgment 退化：(1) attention pattern 在长序列中分布更均匀，activation magnitude\\n排序改变，predictor 学到的 \\\"哪些 neuron 重要\\\" 部分失效；(2) Llama 3.1 8B 使用 RoPE 位置编码，\\n支持 128K 但 2048 训练的 predictor 未见过长距离 dependency pattern，导致 long-range QA 任务退化最严重\\n（single-doc QA -46%）；(3) Summarization 相对保留（-20%），因为 extractive 倾向——保留 high-magnitude\\nneurons 即可抓住 salient sentences，不依赖 fine-grained neuron interaction。\\n\\nKL 30% vs BCE+comp 30% 差距仅 1.1 分（14.0 vs 12.9），因为长序列评估中 predictor 的 mask quality\\n优势被序列长度 generalization gap 部分抵消。BCE+comp 的 compensation MLP 在长序列中反而可能提供\\n额外的 error correction（因为它在推理时修补 per-layer error，与序列长度无关），部分弥补了 BCE 的\\nweaker mask。这进一步模糊了 \\\"KL eliminates compensation\\\" 的实际意义。\\n\\nDense baseline 本身分数偏低（overall 23.0），反映 Llama 3.1 8B base model 在 long-context generation\\ntasks 上的固有局限（非 instruction-tuned）。低 baseline 使得 relative degradation 看起来更严重，\\n但 absolute 差异小——审稿人可能质疑 evaluation 的 informative value。\\n\"\n181\t  },\n182\t  {\n183\t    \"name\": \"mtbench_evaluation\",\n184\t    \"description\": \"MT-Bench 80 题多轮评估（GPT-4o judge），8 categories。测试 sparsity 对 instruction-following\\n和 multi-turn coherence 的影响。需要 instruction-tuned model 或 base model 的 few-shot prompting。\\n\",\n185\t    \"results\": {\n186\t      \"dense_overall\": 3.8,\n187\t      \"dense_writing\": 4.5,\n188\t      \"dense_roleplay\": 4.2,\n189\t      \"dense_reasoning\": 3.5,\n190\t      \"dense_math\": 2.0,\n191\t      \"dense_coding\": 3.8,\n192\t      \"dense_extraction\": 5.0,\n193\t      \"dense_stem\": 3.2,\n194\t      \"dense_humanities\": 4.2,\n195\t      \"kl30_uniform_overall\": 2.9,\n196\t      \"kl30_uniform_drop_vs_dense\": -0.9,\n197\t      \"kl30_uniform_drop_pct\": -23.7,\n198\t      \"kl50_overall\": 1.8,\n199\t      \"kl50_drop_pct\": -52.6,\n200\t      \"bce_comp30_overall\": 2.7,\n201\t      \"teal30_overall\": 2.4,\n202\t      \"base_model_discriminative_power\": \"low — dense baseline 3.8 已接近 floor，sparsity 条件间差异被压缩\",\n203\t      \"worst_category_kl30\": \"math (1.2, -40% vs dense 2.0)\",\n204\t      \"evaluation_cost\": \"需要 GPT-4o API, ~$15-20 per full evaluation\"\n205\t    },\n206\t    \"tables\": [\n207\t      \"Table 6 (Appendix): MT-Bench Scores by Category（8 categories × 5 conditions）\"\n208\t    ],\n209\t    \"figures\": [],\n210\t    \"analysis\": \"MT-Bench 在 worst case 下基本无用：base model baseline 太低（3.8），sparsity 条件间差异 <1 分，\\n审稿人不会从这个评估中获得有价值的信息。建议：(1) 从论文中删除或仅在 appendix 一句话带过；\\n(2) 如果 reviewer 明确要求 multi-turn evaluation，说明 \\\"base model limitation, instruct model\\nevaluation requires predictor transfer study which is out of scope\\\"；(3) 将 plan_011 的 4 GPU hours\\n和 API cost 重新分配。\\n唯一可能的叙事价值：证明 \\\"即使在最不利的评估条件下（low-baseline, multi-turn），KL 仍 ≥ TEAL\\\"，\\n但这是一个极弱的 claim。\\n\\n\\nLlama 3.1 8B base model 在 MT-Bench 上的 dense score 仅 ~3.8（instruct 版本 ~7.5），因为 base model\\n不擅长 instruction following 和 multi-turn dialogue。在如此低的 baseline 上，sparsity 造成的额外退化\\n被 floor effect 压缩——即使 50% sparsity 的 score（1.8）也只比 dense（3.8）低 2.0 分，而 instruct 模型\\n上相同 sparsity 可能造成 3–4 分的下降。\\n\\n结果的信息量极低：所有条件都在 1.5–4.0 分区间内，差异可能在 judge model 的评分 noise 范围内。\\nMath 和 STEM 类别退化最严重（floor 更明显），writing 和 humanities 相对保留。\\nKL 30% vs BCE+comp 30% 差异仅 0.2 分，统计不显著。\\n\\n如果使用 instruct model（需额外配置 predictor 迁移），结果会更有区分度，但引入了 \\\"base-trained predictor\\non instruct model\\\" 的 domain shift 问题。\\n\"\n211\t  },\n212\t  {\n213\t    \"name\": \"ruler_evaluation\",\n214\t    \"description\": \"RULER synthetic long-context evaluation at 4K 和 16K context length，3 task types\\n（NIAH, Variable Tracking, Common/Frequent Words）。测试 predictor 在结构化长序列任务上的泛化。\\n\",\n215\t    \"results\": {\n216\t      \"dense_4k_niah\": 92.0,\n217\t      \"dense_4k_vt\": 78.0,\n218\t      \"dense_4k_cw\": 85.0,\n219\t      \"dense_4k_avg\": 85.0,\n220\t      \"kl30_4k_niah\": 75.0,\n221\t      \"kl30_4k_vt\": 60.0,\n222\t      \"kl30_4k_cw\": 70.0,\n223\t      \"kl30_4k_avg\": 68.3,\n224\t      \"kl30_4k_retention\": 0.8,\n225\t      \"kl50_4k_niah\": 42.0,\n226\t      \"kl50_4k_vt\": 28.0,\n227\t      \"kl50_4k_cw\": 38.0,\n228\t      \"kl50_4k_avg\": 36.0,\n229\t      \"kl50_4k_retention\": 0.42,\n230\t      \"dense_16k_niah\": 85.0,\n231\t      \"dense_16k_vt\": 62.0,\n232\t      \"dense_16k_cw\": 72.0,\n233\t      \"dense_16k_avg\": 73.0,\n234\t      \"kl30_16k_niah\": 48.0,\n235\t      \"kl30_16k_vt\": 30.0,\n236\t      \"kl30_16k_cw\": 42.0,\n237\t      \"kl30_16k_avg\": 40.0,\n238\t      \"kl30_16k_retention\": 0.55,\n239\t      \"kl50_16k_niah\": 18.0,\n240\t      \"kl50_16k_vt\": 12.0,\n241\t      \"kl50_16k_cw\": 15.0,\n242\t      \"kl50_16k_avg\": 15.0,\n243\t      \"kl50_16k_retention\": 0.21,\n244\t      \"kl30_retention_4k_to_16k_drop\": -0.25,\n245\t      \"kl50_retention_4k_to_16k_drop\": -0.21,\n246\t      \"dense_retention_4k_to_16k\": 0.86\n247\t    },\n248\t    \"tables\": [\n249\t      \"Table 7 (Appendix): RULER Results at 4K and 16K（3 task types × 3 sparsity levels × 2 context lengths）\"\n250\t    ],\n251\t    \"figures\": [],\n252\t    \"analysis\": \"RULER 结果确认了 worst-case 的 predictor length generalization 问题：超出训练长度 4× 以上，\\nretention 从 80% 骤降至 55%（30%）和 21%（50%）。这是一个 honest limitation，但需要正确\\nframe：(1) 所有 sparse inference 方法都面临 length generalization 问题，不是 KL-specific；\\n(2) 解决方案是 longer training sequences（直接但 GPU-expensive）或 length-adaptive predictor\\n（future work）；(3) 在论文中作为 limitation 明确讨论，不隐藏。\\n对论文影响：(1) RULER 数据不进入 main body，放 appendix；(2) 在 Limitation section 引用 RULER 结果\\n说明 \\\"current predictor design assumes fixed-length training and degrades at 4× training length\\\"；\\n(3) 建议 future work 方向：mixed-length training 或 length-invariant predictor architecture。\\nplan_012 的 P2 优先级在 worst case 下进一步降低——如果 deadline 紧张，完全可以 skip 并在\\nlimitation 中声明 \\\"long-context evaluation is left for future work\\\"。\\n\\nRULER 的 NIAH 任务要求模型精确定位特定位置的信息——这对 neuron pruning 极度敏感，因为 attention-to-FFN\\n的 information routing 被 mask 截断。4K 时 predictor 尚可（训练长度 2048 的 2× 内），retention 80%。\\n但 16K 时（训练长度的 8×），predictor 的 neuron importance judgment 严重失准：长序列中 attention 分布\\n变化导致 FFN activation pattern 完全不同于训练分布，predictor 选择了错误的 neuron 保留。\\n\\nVariable Tracking 是最受影响的任务类型——需要跨 token 的持续 state tracking，而 sparse FFN 打断了\\nintermediate representation 的 continuity。50% sparsity @ 16K 的 12% accuracy 接近 random（基于\\ncandidate pool size）。\\n\\n相对于 LongBench（基于 F1/ROUGE 的 generation 评估），RULER 的 accuracy-based 评估更尖锐地暴露了\\npredictor 的 length generalization 失败。但问题在于：这是 ALL sparse methods 的共同问题（training-free\\nTEAL 在长序列上同样退化），不是 KL-specific 的。没有 TEAL/BCE baseline 的 RULER 数据，审稿人无法\\n判断 KL 是否比 alternative 更好。\\n\"\n253\t  }\n254\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a65ea5d-7d8b-45ad-b79b-73646d535216","uuid":"f0e1b608-02fb-43f1-a907-cf919c255822","timestamp":"2026-05-18T18:19:27.909Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T173518/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"c1_ablation_replication_3seed\",\n    \"description\": \"C1 causal ablation 的 s123 retry 和 s456 新实验。训练 BCE predictor 使用各 seed 的 KL-derived oracle mask 作为 target，\\n在 TEAL uniform 50% 协议下评估，与对应 seed 的 KL predictor 对比。验证 s42 exact match 是否跨 seed 复现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"s123_bce_kl_targets_ppl_teal_uniform_50pct\": 12.71,\n      \"s123_kl_reference_ppl_teal_uniform_50pct\": 11.86,\n      \"s123_ppl_delta\": 0.85,\n      \"s123_oracle_agreement\": 0.921,\n      \"s123_train_bce_loss\": 0.072,\n      \"s123_arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.345,\n      \"s123_winogrande_acc\": 0.598,\n      \"s123_mmlu_acc\": 0.253,\n      \"s123_gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.015,\n      \"s123_downstream_ref_arc_c\": 0.379,\n      \"s123_downstream_ref_wg\": 0.622,\n      \"s123_downstream_ref_mmlu\": 0.278,\n      \"s123_downstream_ref_gsm8k\": 0.024,\n      \"s123_max_downstream_delta_pp\": 3.4,\n      \"s456_bce_kl_targets_ppl_teal_uniform_50pct\": 12.55,\n      \"s456_kl_reference_ppl_teal_uniform_50pct\": 11.95,\n      \"s456_ppl_delta\": 0.6,\n      \"s456_oracle_agreement\": 0.943,\n      \"s456_train_bce_loss\": 0.063,\n      \"s456_arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.362,\n      \"s456_winogrande_acc\": 0.612,\n      \"s456_mmlu_acc\": 0.268,\n      \"s456_gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.019,\n      \"s456_max_downstream_delta_pp\": 2.1,\n      \"three_seed_ppl_deltas\": [\n        0.0,\n        0.85,\n        0.6\n      ],\n      \"three_seed_ppl_delta_mean\": 0.48,\n      \"three_seed_ppl_delta_std\": 0.36,\n      \"three_seed_oracle_agreement_mean\": 0.947,\n      \"three_seed_oracle_agreement_std\": 0.024,\n      \"three_seed_max_downstream_delta_pp\": 3.4,\n      \"gradient_coupling_contribution_range_pct\": \"0–18%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3: C1 Causal Ablation（3 seeds，PPL + 4 downstream tasks，含 oracle agreement）\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C1 从 \\\"clean decomposition proving gradient coupling = 0\\\" 降级为 \\\"target quality is dominant but gradient coupling\\ncontribution is seed-dependent (0–18%)\\\"。论文需要：(1) 诚实报告 3 seed 及 variance；(2) 放弃 \\\"sole driver\\\" 措辞，\\n改为 \\\"primary driver, explaining 82–100% of advantage\\\"；(3) 将 seed 依赖性本身作为 finding 讨论——mask landscape\\n的局部结构决定了 gradient coupling 的边际贡献。C1 仍有价值（first attempt at causal decomposition for sparsity\\npredictor training loss），但 novelty 从 \\\"empirical discovery\\\" 降为 \\\"informative ablation with nuanced outcome\\\"。\\n审稿人会说 \\\"interesting but not conclusive\\\"。\\n\\n\\ns42 的 exact match（Δ=0.00）是 seed-specific 的幸运结果：s42 的 KL predictor 收敛到的局部最优产生了\\n\\\"clean\\\" mask pattern——borderline zone（gate probability 0.4–0.6）的 neuron 比例低（~8%），使 BCE 的\\nfactorized loss 足以高精度复制。s123 的 KL predictor 收敛到了不同局部最优，borderline neuron 比例更高（~14%），\\n这些 neuron 的重要性依赖于与其他 neuron 的共激活模式（joint interaction），BCE 无法捕捉。oracle agreement\\n从 0.978 降至 0.921，6% 的 mask 分歧集中在 knowledge-critical 中间层（L12–L20），导致 ARC-c 推理任务\\n出现 3.4pp gap。s456 介于两者之间（agreement 0.943，Δ=0.60），表明 gradient coupling 贡献是 loss landscape\\n局部结构的函数。3-seed 平均 Δ=0.48 技术上 <0.5，但 s123 的 0.85 无法被 error bar 掩盖，审稿人会质疑\\n\\\"gradient coupling = 0\\\" 的普遍性声明。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bce_30pct_forced_topk_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"BCE predictor（trained at 30% target on Llama-3.1-8B）通过 forced TEAL top-k 在 30% uniform sparsity 下评估。\\n填充 Table 2 的 BCE 30% operating point 数据。对比 KL 30% uniform（PPL 8.82）和 TEAL 30%（PPL 10.97）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"wikitext2_ppl_teal_uniform_30pct\": 9.15,\n      \"gap_vs_kl30_uniform\": 0.33,\n      \"gap_vs_teal30\": -1.82,\n      \"arc_challenge_acc_norm\": 0.401,\n      \"winogrande_acc\": 0.668,\n      \"mmlu_acc\": 0.378,\n      \"gsm8k_exact_match\": 0.062,\n      \"ref_kl30_uniform_ppl\": 8.82,\n      \"ref_kl30_uniform_mmlu\": 0.385,\n      \"ref_kl30_uniform_arc_c\": 0.443,\n      \"ref_kl30_uniform_wg\": 0.692,\n      \"mmlu_gap_vs_kl30_pp\": -0.7,\n      \"arc_c_gap_vs_kl30_pp\": -4.2,\n      \"wg_gap_vs_kl30_pp\": -2.4,\n      \"predictor_native_sparsity\": 0.295,\n      \"lagrangian_converged\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Recommended Operating Point Comparison（30% sparsity, all methods）\",\n      \"Table 1: Main Results（增加 BCE 30% 行）\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"BCE 30% PPL 9.15 vs KL 8.82（Δ=0.33, 3.7%）在 recommended operating point 实质追平。这削弱了 \\\"KL discovers\\nfundamentally different masks\\\" 作为 practical advantage 的叙事——在用户最可能部署的 sparsity level 上，\\n简单的 BCE + magnitude oracle 就足够好。KL 的优势主要体现在 ≥40% 的高 sparsity 区间，而该区间的 downstream\\ncollapse（MMLU ~31%）使其本身缺乏部署价值。\\nReframe: KL 的价值不在于 \\\"better masks at all sparsity levels\\\"，而在于 (a) 自动发现 good mask（zero-shot,\\n无需预定义 oracle），(b) 在高 sparsity 区间提供 graceful degradation 而非 catastrophic collapse，\\n(c) 跨 sparsity level 的 single training recipe（一个 KL predictor 可在 30–50% 间灵活部署，而 BCE 需要\\nper-level oracle 设计）。\\n\\n\\n30% sparsity 下 magnitude-based mask 与 optimal mask 的重合度远高于 50%（Jaccard ~0.6 vs ~0.4），因为\\n需要剪除的 neuron 大多是 \\\"trivially unimportant\\\"（activation magnitude 极低 + gate probability 极低），\\nBCE 和 KL 在这些 easy case 上完全一致。KL 的 joint interaction 优势只在 borderline neurons 上体现，而\\n30% 时 borderline zone 极窄（仅需剪除最不重要的 30%，几乎没有 hard decision）。PPL gap 从 50% 时的\\n~14 PPL（22.51 vs 8.82, 对比 BCE 50% vs KL 30%）收缩到 30% 时的 0.33，确认 KL-BCE delta 随 sparsity\\n近似二次收缩。BCE Lagrangian 在 8B 30% target 下正常收敛（不像 Qwen-14B 的 collapse），因为 30%\\n目标松弛、loss landscape smooth。下游任务 gap 最大 4.2pp（ARC-c），在 3-seed KL variance 范围内。\\n审稿人会看到 Table 2 中 KL 和 BCE 在 recommended operating point 几乎没有差别，质疑 KL 的实际部署价值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\",\n    \"description\": \"KL predictor 在 25%/30%/35%/40%/45%/50% 六个 sparsity level 的 TEAL uniform 评估。\\n使用各 level 的 dedicated predictor（25/35/45 为新训练，30/40/50 复用已有）。\\n生成 regime curve 并尝试识别 regime boundary。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ppl_25pct\": 8.9,\n      \"ppl_30pct\": 8.82,\n      \"ppl_35pct\": 8.55,\n      \"ppl_40pct\": 8.36,\n      \"ppl_45pct\": 10.25,\n      \"ppl_50pct\": 11.96,\n      \"monotonicity_violations_ppl\": 3,\n      \"ppl_global_25pct\": 9.05,\n      \"ppl_global_30pct\": 8.98,\n      \"ppl_global_35pct\": 8.7,\n      \"ppl_global_40pct\": 10.12,\n      \"ppl_global_45pct\": 10.9,\n      \"ppl_global_50pct\": 11.79,\n      \"monotonicity_violations_ppl_global\": 2,\n      \"mmlu_25pct\": 0.39,\n      \"mmlu_30pct\": 0.406,\n      \"mmlu_35pct\": 0.415,\n      \"mmlu_40pct\": 0.307,\n      \"mmlu_45pct\": 0.282,\n      \"mmlu_50pct\": 0.278,\n      \"mmlu_monotonicity_violations\": 2,\n      \"arc_c_25pct\": 0.43,\n      \"arc_c_30pct\": 0.408,\n      \"arc_c_35pct\": 0.44,\n      \"arc_c_40pct\": 0.418,\n      \"arc_c_45pct\": 0.35,\n      \"arc_c_50pct\": 0.328,\n      \"arc_c_monotonicity_violations\": 3,\n      \"winogrande_25pct\": 0.7,\n      \"winogrande_30pct\": 0.686,\n      \"winogrande_35pct\": 0.705,\n      \"winogrande_40pct\": 0.672,\n      \"winogrande_45pct\": 0.64,\n      \"winogrande_50pct\": 0.629,\n      \"winogrande_monotonicity_violations\": 2,\n      \"gsm8k_25pct\": 0.082,\n      \"gsm8k_30pct\": 0.074,\n      \"gsm8k_35pct\": 0.065,\n      \"gsm8k_40pct\": 0.039,\n      \"gsm8k_45pct\": 0.022,\n      \"gsm8k_50pct\": 0.021,\n      \"ppl_cliff_location\": \"40–45%\",\n      \"mmlu_cliff_location\": \"35–40%\",\n      \"cliff_dissociation\": \"PPL 和 MMLU 的 cliff 位于不同 sparsity level，间隔约 5pp\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: 6-Point Sparsity Regime Analysis（PPL + 4 downstream, uniform + global allocation）\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Regime analysis 从 Claim 3 的核心贡献降级为 supplementary empirical characterization。原始叙事\\n\\\"three discrete regimes (budget-surplus / budget-constrained / capacity-cliff) with non-monotonic allocation\\npreference\\\" 被替换为：(a) continuous degradation with a PPL sweet spot around 35–40%；(b) PPL-downstream\\ndissociation 作为 finding（PPL cliff at 40–45%, MMLU cliff at 35–40%）；(c) practical recommendation\\n不变（30% uniform），但理由从 \\\"optimal regime 1 operating point\\\" 改为 \\\"safety margin below cliff\\\"。\\nNon-monotonicity 可 spin 为 \\\"dedicated-predictor optimization effect\\\"（each sparsity level has its own\\ntraining sweet spot），但审稿人可能视为 experimental noise 或 Lagrangian artifact。\\n建议在论文中补充 3-seed bars at 30/50 以佐证 known points 的 stability，并坦承 single-seed sweep\\n限制了 statistical confidence。\\n\\n\\nPPL 非单调性（25→40% 持续下降）的机制：dedicated predictor 在中等 sparsity（35–40%）达到 loss-sparsity 的\\n最佳平衡——Lagrangian 约束满足良好（actual sparsity 接近 target），KL loss 有足够的 \\\"budget\\\" 学习 nuanced\\nmask pattern。25% 时 predictor undertrained（actual 23%, lambda 打满 5000 仍不够），mask 质量反而不如\\n30% 的 well-calibrated predictor。35% 时 predictor 在 sweet spot（actual 33.6%, loss 收敛良好），\\n产生了比 30% 更优的 neuron ranking。40% 沿用 50%-trained predictor at 40% uniform（d030 数据），\\n该 predictor 在 40% 时仍有余量因此 PPL 最低。\\n\\n45→50% 的急剧上升反映 capacity cliff——不是 allocation 问题（都用 uniform），而是 model 容量不足。\\n但 MMLU 的 cliff 出现在 35→40%（Δ=10.8pp），比 PPL cliff（40→45%）早一个档位。这反映 knowledge-intensive\\ntasks（MMLU）对 neuron 缺失的敏感度高于 perplexity——PPL 可以靠 redistributing probability mass 补偿，\\n但 factual recall 一旦关键 neuron 被剪就不可逆。\\n\\n3 处 PPL monotonicity violation 使 \\\"three discrete regimes with phase transitions\\\" 叙事不可持续：\\n没有从 regime 1 到 regime 2 的 clean boundary，整个 25–40% 区间是一个 non-monotonic plateau。\\n审稿人会质疑 \\\"regime\\\" 分类的 principled basis。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"longbench_full_evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"LongBench English subset（14 tasks, 4K–32K tokens）评估所有条件：KL 30% uniform, KL 50%,\\nBCE+comp 30%, TEAL 30%, TEAL 50%, Dense。测试 predictor 在超出训练序列长度（2048）时的泛化能力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_single_doc_qa_avg\": 10.8,\n      \"dense_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 18.5,\n      \"dense_summarization_avg\": 18.2,\n      \"dense_few_shot_avg\": 36.0,\n      \"dense_code_avg\": 31.5,\n      \"dense_overall_avg\": 23.0,\n      \"kl30_single_doc_qa_avg\": 5.8,\n      \"kl30_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 9.5,\n      \"kl30_summarization_avg\": 14.5,\n      \"kl30_few_shot_avg\": 21.0,\n      \"kl30_code_avg\": 19.0,\n      \"kl30_overall_avg\": 14.0,\n      \"kl30_retention_vs_dense\": 0.61,\n      \"kl50_single_doc_qa_avg\": 2.2,\n      \"kl50_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 3.8,\n      \"kl50_summarization_avg\": 8.5,\n      \"kl50_few_shot_avg\": 8.5,\n      \"kl50_code_avg\": 9.0,\n      \"kl50_overall_avg\": 6.4,\n      \"kl50_retention_vs_dense\": 0.28,\n      \"bce_comp_30_single_doc_qa_avg\": 5.2,\n      \"bce_comp_30_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 8.8,\n      \"bce_comp_30_summarization_avg\": 13.5,\n      \"bce_comp_30_few_shot_avg\": 19.5,\n      \"bce_comp_30_code_avg\": 17.5,\n      \"bce_comp_30_overall_avg\": 12.9,\n      \"bce_comp_30_retention_vs_dense\": 0.56,\n      \"teal30_single_doc_qa_avg\": 4.2,\n      \"teal30_multi_doc_qa_avg\": 7.2,\n      \"teal30_summarization_avg\": 11.5,\n      \"teal30_few_shot_avg\": 16.0,\n      \"teal30_code_avg\": 15.0,\n      \"teal30_overall_avg\": 10.8,\n      \"teal30_retention_vs_dense\": 0.47,\n      \"teal50_overall_avg\": 3.8,\n      \"teal50_retention_vs_dense\": 0.17,\n      \"kl30_vs_bce_comp30_delta\": 1.1,\n      \"kl30_vs_teal30_delta\": 3.2,\n      \"worst_category_kl30\": \"single-doc QA (-46%)\",\n      \"best_category_kl30\": \"summarization (-20%)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: LongBench Results by Task Category（5 categories × 6 conditions, retention % vs dense）\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"LongBench 结果 mixed：KL > TEAL（training-free）confirmed，但 KL vs BCE+comp 差异在 long-context 上\\n被压缩到不显著水平。Dense baseline 偏低限制了评估的 discriminative power。\\n对论文的影响：(1) 不宜作为 main contribution，降为 appendix 或简要提及；(2) 如果 reviewer 要求\\nlong-context evaluation，可呈现但需坦承 base model limitation 和 predictor generalization gap；\\n(3) 建议补充 \\\"predictor seq-len generalization\\\" 分析（对比 2048 vs 4096 训练长度的 predictor 在\\nLongBench 上的差异），但 GPU budget 可能不允许。\\n实际影响：plan_010 的 P1 优先级在 worst case 下应降为 P2，将 GPU hours 重新分配给更能 strengthen\\nnarrative 的实验（如 BCE 30% 的多 seed 验证）。\\n\\n\\nPredictor 在 2048 tokens 上训练，LongBench 任务平均 8K–16K tokens。超出训练长度后 predictor 的\\nneuron importance judgment 退化：(1) attention pattern 在长序列中分布更均匀，activation magnitude\\n排序改变，predictor 学到的 \\\"哪些 neuron 重要\\\" 部分失效；(2) Llama 3.1 8B 使用 RoPE 位置编码，\\n支持 128K 但 2048 训练的 predictor 未见过长距离 dependency pattern，导致 long-range QA 任务退化最严重\\n（single-doc QA -46%）；(3) Summarization 相对保留（-20%），因为 extractive 倾向——保留 high-magnitude\\nneurons 即可抓住 salient sentences，不依赖 fine-grained neuron interaction。\\n\\nKL 30% vs BCE+comp 30% 差距仅 1.1 分（14.0 vs 12.9），因为长序列评估中 predictor 的 mask quality\\n优势被序列长度 generalization gap 部分抵消。BCE+comp 的 compensation MLP 在长序列中反而可能提供\\n额外的 error correction（因为它在推理时修补 per-layer error，与序列长度无关），部分弥补了 BCE 的\\nweaker mask。这进一步模糊了 \\\"KL eliminates compensation\\\" 的实际意义。\\n\\nDense baseline 本身分数偏低（overall 23.0），反映 Llama 3.1 8B base model 在 long-context generation\\ntasks 上的固有局限（非 instruction-tuned）。低 baseline 使得 relative degradation 看起来更严重，\\n但 absolute 差异小——审稿人可能质疑 evaluation 的 informative value。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"mtbench_evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"MT-Bench 80 题多轮评估（GPT-4o judge），8 categories。测试 sparsity 对 instruction-following\\n和 multi-turn coherence 的影响。需要 instruction-tuned model 或 base model 的 few-shot prompting。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_overall\": 3.8,\n      \"dense_writing\": 4.5,\n      \"dense_roleplay\": 4.2,\n      \"dense_reasoning\": 3.5,\n      \"dense_math\": 2.0,\n      \"dense_coding\": 3.8,\n      \"dense_extraction\": 5.0,\n      \"dense_stem\": 3.2,\n      \"dense_humanities\": 4.2,\n      \"kl30_uniform_overall\": 2.9,\n      \"kl30_uniform_drop_vs_dense\": -0.9,\n      \"kl30_uniform_drop_pct\": -23.7,\n      \"kl50_overall\": 1.8,\n      \"kl50_drop_pct\": -52.6,\n      \"bce_comp30_overall\": 2.7,\n      \"teal30_overall\": 2.4,\n      \"base_model_discriminative_power\": \"low — dense baseline 3.8 已接近 floor，sparsity 条件间差异被压缩\",\n      \"worst_category_kl30\": \"math (1.2, -40% vs dense 2.0)\",\n      \"evaluation_cost\": \"需要 GPT-4o API, ~$15-20 per full evaluation\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6 (Appendix): MT-Bench Scores by Category（8 categories × 5 conditions）\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MT-Bench 在 worst case 下基本无用：base model baseline 太低（3.8），sparsity 条件间差异 <1 分，\\n审稿人不会从这个评估中获得有价值的信息。建议：(1) 从论文中删除或仅在 appendix 一句话带过；\\n(2) 如果 reviewer 明确要求 multi-turn evaluation，说明 \\\"base model limitation, instruct model\\nevaluation requires predictor transfer study which is out of scope\\\"；(3) 将 plan_011 的 4 GPU hours\\n和 API cost 重新分配。\\n唯一可能的叙事价值：证明 \\\"即使在最不利的评估条件下（low-baseline, multi-turn），KL 仍 ≥ TEAL\\\"，\\n但这是一个极弱的 claim。\\n\\n\\nLlama 3.1 8B base model 在 MT-Bench 上的 dense score 仅 ~3.8（instruct 版本 ~7.5），因为 base model\\n不擅长 instruction following 和 multi-turn dialogue。在如此低的 baseline 上，sparsity 造成的额外退化\\n被 floor effect 压缩——即使 50% sparsity 的 score（1.8）也只比 dense（3.8）低 2.0 分，而 instruct 模型\\n上相同 sparsity 可能造成 3–4 分的下降。\\n\\n结果的信息量极低：所有条件都在 1.5–4.0 分区间内，差异可能在 judge model 的评分 noise 范围内。\\nMath 和 STEM 类别退化最严重（floor 更明显），writing 和 humanities 相对保留。\\nKL 30% vs BCE+comp 30% 差异仅 0.2 分，统计不显著。\\n\\n如果使用 instruct model（需额外配置 predictor 迁移），结果会更有区分度，但引入了 \\\"base-trained predictor\\non instruct model\\\" 的 domain shift 问题。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ruler_evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"RULER synthetic long-context evaluation at 4K 和 16K context length，3 task types\\n（NIAH, Variable Tracking, Common/Frequent Words）。测试 predictor 在结构化长序列任务上的泛化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_4k_niah\": 92.0,\n      \"dense_4k_vt\": 78.0,\n      \"dense_4k_cw\": 85.0,\n      \"dense_4k_avg\": 85.0,\n      \"kl30_4k_niah\": 75.0,\n      \"kl30_4k_vt\": 60.0,\n      \"kl30_4k_cw\": 70.0,\n      \"kl30_4k_avg\": 68.3,\n      \"kl30_4k_retention\": 0.8,\n      \"kl50_4k_niah\": 42.0,\n      \"kl50_4k_vt\": 28.0,\n      \"kl50_4k_cw\": 38.0,\n      \"kl50_4k_avg\": 36.0,\n      \"kl50_4k_retention\": 0.42,\n      \"dense_16k_niah\": 85.0,\n      \"dense_16k_vt\": 62.0,\n      \"dense_16k_cw\": 72.0,\n      \"dense_16k_avg\": 73.0,\n      \"kl30_16k_niah\": 48.0,\n      \"kl30_16k_vt\": 30.0,\n      \"kl30_16k_cw\": 42.0,\n      \"kl30_16k_avg\": 40.0,\n      \"kl30_16k_retention\": 0.55,\n      \"kl50_16k_niah\": 18.0,\n      \"kl50_16k_vt\": 12.0,\n      \"kl50_16k_cw\": 15.0,\n      \"kl50_16k_avg\": 15.0,\n      \"kl50_16k_retention\": 0.21,\n      \"kl30_retention_4k_to_16k_drop\": -0.25,\n      \"kl50_retention_4k_to_16k_drop\": -0.21,\n      \"dense_retention_4k_to_16k\": 0.86\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 (Appendix): RULER Results at 4K and 16K（3 task types × 3 sparsity levels × 2 context lengths）\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RULER 结果确认了 worst-case 的 predictor length generalization 问题：超出训练长度 4× 以上，\\nretention 从 80% 骤降至 55%（30%）和 21%（50%）。这是一个 honest limitation，但需要正确\\nframe：(1) 所有 sparse inference 方法都面临 length generalization 问题，不是 KL-specific；\\n(2) 解决方案是 longer training sequences（直接但 GPU-expensive）或 length-adaptive predictor\\n（future work）；(3) 在论文中作为 limitation 明确讨论，不隐藏。\\n对论文影响：(1) RULER 数据不进入 main body，放 appendix；(2) 在 Limitation section 引用 RULER 结果\\n说明 \\\"current predictor design assumes fixed-length training and degrades at 4× training length\\\"；\\n(3) 建议 future work 方向：mixed-length training 或 length-invariant predictor architecture。\\nplan_012 的 P2 优先级在 worst case 下进一步降低——如果 deadline 紧张，完全可以 skip 并在\\nlimitation 中声明 \\\"long-context evaluation is left for future work\\\"。\\n\\nRULER 的 NIAH 任务要求模型精确定位特定位置的信息——这对 neuron pruning 极度敏感，因为 attention-to-FFN\\n的 information routing 被 mask 截断。4K 时 predictor 尚可（训练长度 2048 的 2× 内），retention 80%。\\n但 16K 时（训练长度的 8×），predictor 的 neuron importance judgment 严重失准：长序列中 attention 分布\\n变化导致 FFN activation pattern 完全不同于训练分布，predictor 选择了错误的 neuron 保留。\\n\\nVariable Tracking 是最受影响的任务类型——需要跨 token 的持续 state tracking，而 sparse FFN 打断了\\nintermediate representation 的 continuity。50% sparsity @ 16K 的 12% accuracy 接近 random（基于\\ncandidate pool size）。\\n\\n相对于 LongBench（基于 F1/ROUGE 的 generation 评估），RULER 的 accuracy-based 评估更尖锐地暴露了\\npredictor 的 length generalization 失败。但问题在于：这是 ALL sparse methods 的共同问题（training-free\\nTEAL 在长序列上同样退化），不是 KL-specific 的。没有 TEAL/BCE baseline 的 RULER 数据，审稿人无法\\n判断 KL 是否比 alternative 更好。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":254,"startLine":1,"totalLines":254}}}
